# ReluLayer™ Root Governance

## Identity & Mission

- Product: **ReluLayer™** — deterministic **Edge Governor** and **Execution Gatekeeper** for autonomous AI agents, LLM tool calling, and Physical Super Intelligence (Physical SI) actuator loops.
- Entity: **Atelier Logic Group LLC dba ReluLayer™** (CAGE `20JX8`, UEI `G9WFN3AL69J3`).
- Canonical baseline: `PRD.md`. Canonical entity identifiers: `Organizations/AtelierLogicGroup/00-governance/entity-identity.md`.
- Never anthropomorphize the kernel (no "reflexes", "thoughts", "instincts", "believes").

## Author Provenance

- All commits authored by `ishmaelamin <ishmael.amin@outlook.com>`.
- No `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: GitHub Copilot`, or bot attribution trailers.
- Conventional Commits only: `docs(prd):`, `feat(core):`, `fix(security):`, `ci(actions):`, etc.

## Dual-Repository Parity

- `/home/iamin/Dist/relulayer-oss` (public mirror) and `/home/iamin/Organizations/ReluLayer` (monorepo) stay synchronized for shared files.
- Mirror identical `PRD.md` and `.cursorrules` content across both repos before pushing.
- Public mirror is open-core only; never copy proprietary monorepo content into it.

## Architectural Non-Negotiables

- `#![no_std]` first for safety-critical crates.
- Zero dynamic heap allocations on hot paths.
- Bounded stack allocations < 1 KB per call.
- Sub-microsecond fast-path latency ceiling.
- Production builds: `panic = "abort"`, `lto = true`, `opt-level = 3`.

## API Contracts

- Action identifiers and payloads are raw `bytes` (`&[u8]` / Python `bytes`).
- Verification failures raise `ValueError` (Python) or return a negative FFI code; never a plain boolean.
- PyO3 0.23+ smart-pointer signatures (`&Bound<'_, PyModule>`).

## SCM Discipline

- Stage explicit paths only; `git add .`, `git add -A`, `git add *` are forbidden.
- Never commit `target/`, `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, build artifacts, compiled dynamic libraries, or Windows `Zone.Identifier` files.
- Verify clean `git status` and run `git diff --stat` before every push.
